  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "The Financial Conduct Authority (FCA) is the statutory regulator of financial services and markets in the United Kingdom, operating independently of government under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000. It supervises conduct in retail and wholesale markets, authorises financial firms, and enforces anti-money-laundering obligations. In the blockchain and digital asset domain, the FCA registers crypto-asset businesses under the Money Laundering Regulations, oversees financial promotions for crypto assets, and implements policy derived from international standards bodies such as the Financial Action Task Force.",
